{"type":"text","timestamp":1794559109455,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf3ca40ffeo8xe1K4g3dtqVO","part":{"id":"prt_1d40edd16002UqN0lRRLoepVK1","sessionID":"ses_e2bf3ca40ffeo8xe1K4g3dtqVO","messageID":"msg_1d40eae34001QpYfi2hLrgC7jj","type":"text","text":"T031 is complete. Both new cases failed before the change on exit 0 and now pass, and all four installed runtimes still report wired.\n\nFiles written:\n\n1. `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs` — replaced the serialized-JSON marker search with a walk over the event's entries and nested `hooks` arrays, collecting each `command` from an entry whose `type` is `command`. A runtime is wired only when a command token `node` is followed by a path ending in the runtime's marker. Rewrote the comment above `eventPayload` to say a mention is not a wired hook.\n2. `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` — added the echo-path case and the description-only case, both expecting `hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json`. Changed the wired case to the real `bash -c 'cd \"$PWD\" && node <marker>'` shape.\n\nReceipts:\n\n- Before the fix, `node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` failed both new cases with `0 !== 1` at lines 79 and 95, because the check printed `ok claude` for both.\n- After the fix, the same command reports tests 5, pass 5, fail 0.\n- `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root .` printed `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor`, `ok devin` and exited 0.\n- `node --check .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs` exited 0.\n- The scoped diff touches only the two named files. Other modified files in `git status` belong to other workers and were left alone. Nothing was committed, pushed or ticked.\n\nNothing is blocked on the operator.","time":{"start":1794559106326,"end":1794559109455}}}
